I walk further in the busy market.
I find a small fruit stall.
There are many baskets in the stall.
The baskets are full of dark red winter apples.
I look at a small bag of apples.
"How much does a small bag cost?" I ask the vendor.
He looks in the basket.
"The price is twenty kroner," he answers.
I look in my bag for money.
I give him a paper note for fifty kroner.
The vendor hands me the bag of apples.
Then he gives me money back.
I get exactly thirty kroner back in coins.
The coins are thick and heavy.
I put the heavy coins down into my coat pocket.
The apples smell very fresh.
I put the bag down into my large shopping bag.
